<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 375.9 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 375.9 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of November 14 raised 375.9 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 733 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 109 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.44 (14.56)	   55.8 (114.4)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.79 (16.89)	   63.3 (144.2)</p>
<p>    12 months		 17.64 (17.75)	  107.9 (105.4)</p>
<p>    24 months		 21.42 (21.58)	  148.9 (568.9)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,555 to the U.S. dollar on Monday from 1,555.5 a week earlier and 1,601 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
